<title>MEXICO: Mexico '97 steel output seen 13.9 tonnes - chamber.</title>
<headline>Mexico '97 steel output seen 13.9 tonnes - chamber.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's National Iron and Steel Industry Chamber (Canacero) said on Thursday that steel production will be 13.9 million tonnes in 1997, a 5.5 percent rise from the previous year.</p>
<p>Steel production in 1996 was 13.17 million tonnes, the chamber said in its twice monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>The chamber estimated 1997 production in various steel products:</p>
<p>    Type			  1997	     1996	Pct Chge</p>
<p>Total Steel		  13,900,000     13,170,007	5.5</p>
<p> Mini-mill		    8,763,785	8,443,528	3.8</p>
<p> Blast furnace		5,136,215	4,726,479	8.7</p>
<p>Semi-finished		 2,549,013	2,382,255	7.0</p>
<p>Total rolled products    11,123,967     10,035,596     10.8</p>
<p> Total flat products	5,480,320	4,784,597     14.5</p>
<p>  Slab			    705,358	  653,109	8.0</p>
<p>  Hot rolled sheet	  2,734,936	2,486,936     10.0</p>
<p>  Cold rolled sheet	 2,040,026	1 645,183     24.0</p>
<p>  Total non-flat products 4,950,489	4,648,252	6.5</p>
<p>  Wire rod		    1,258,354	1,233,681	2.0</p>
<p>  Corrugated bar	    2,630,410	2,435,565	8.0</p>
<p>  Commercial shapes	   323,520	  294,110     10.0</p>
<p>  Structural size shapes    342,582	  340,877	0.5</p>
<p>  Bars			    395,622	  344,019     15.0</p>
<p>  Seamless pipe		 693,159	  602,747     15.0</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
